  "native_and_source_review": {
    "canonical_native_bodies": "Only the complete canonical 8001D944 (304 bytes) and 8001DA74 (404 bytes) bodies were independently disassembled and inspected for this review; targets stayed read-only.",
    "actual_abi": "1D944 takes one object pointer plus one genuine float, transferred from a1 to f12. 1DA74 takes the object pointer plus five genuine floats: a1/a2, the a3 home slot at old sp+12, and old sp+16/+20; its result is a real zero/one. No formals, padding, keepers or helper implementations were added.",
    "native_layout": "The object group key is at +56; O32 groups are 12 bytes, small nodes 12 bytes, large nodes 28 bytes. Three distinct fixed arrays have 32 entries each, with separately located byte counters. Types, declarations, field order and formals are byte-identical to each frozen baseline.",
    "small_list": "Stable ascending insertion uses distance < current->distance. Small insertion has no native capacity check: small pool count must be below32; a new group requires group count below32, and otherwise counts stay within0..32.",
    "large_list": "An existing head remains the anchor. Traversal tests current->next before current->distance < distance, so insertion is always after a visited node. The32-group failure comes before group creation; a newly created group remains created if the subsequent32-node capacity check fails. The native reload of the large-pool count after linking is retained in every source.",
    "alias_domain": "All traversed nodes are valid allocated acyclic lists; the next free node is not already linked. The emitter object, group array and both node arrays are distinct valid objects. Shared heads between groups are allowed. Within this domain, rereading nonvolatile next pointers without intervening writes/calls is equivalent, and tail reordering writes independent locations. No concurrency/data-race or arbitrary FCSR guarantee is claimed.",
    "tail_store_order": "Small native tail writes next, object, counter, then distance in the return delay slot; its donor-tail control changes only the three compiled store-order sites. Large native tail writes object, first float, counter, distance, fourth float, second float and third float. The donor-tail source changes natural field sequencing and places count postincrement in the final distance store; all five actual float values and final state are preserved.",
    "float_qualification": "Ordered less-than behavior is preserved, including tested quiet NaN and infinity fixtures under the ordinary engine FP state; exceptional signaling-NaN/FCSR behavior is not overclaimed.",
    "full_state_tests": "The added420 cases cover nonconsecutive links, shared group heads, last-free-slot insertion,32-group and full-pool failure, all five float inputs, emitter bytes, all group/large-node storage and the unrelated small-node pool."
  },
